Possibly the most notable thing about this one is that I started it on
Boxing Day, got to Rodney in a couple of days, then forgot about it
for a while, and then was too scared to play it in case I forgot
something important and died.

At this stage, I remember not much from the early game. I'd like to
thank whoever it was on #nethack who convinced me my XL 10 Valk could
take on the polymorph-trap generated Aleax in the mines.

Getting the Amulet proved to be slightly tricky: I carefully /oTele
and levitated through the graveyard in the Sanctum, but still faced a
vast horde by the time I got to the other side. The reasons for this
became obvious later... killed the High Priest, but he didn't have the
Amulet. Killed the Double Trouble Rodney, but he gave me only
something which fitted into my bag. At this point I was in the midst
of a load of nasty monsters and burning my way through my
!oFH. Yeenoghu was around, but killing him was tricky as he kept
running away to the stairs. A quick bit of research (thanks again
#nethack and the source) convinced me he must have the Amulet, so used
my carefully prepared c!oGL to escape the Sanctum, back down the
stairs, whacked on Yeenoghu and picked up an Amulet which very
thankfully couldn't be confined.

After that, it was plain sailing. The most embarrassing bit was
discovering half way through the ascension run that I didn't have my
boots of speed on. Ooops (and explains why the Sanctum was able to
fill up so much...).

Astral was a breeze: whacked on Death (didn't touch me) and the first
Altar was to Odin. Used up my final two wishes on a blessed christmas
pudding and a blessed figurine of a woodchuck :-)

